Ah; gotcha.  I haven't had the time to keep tabs on r.g.r.n for many 
months, so I never knew about that post.

The contents of the two deaths files are all entries that have been 
logged during the Tournament, but not necessarily with the most recent 
version of NetHack.  It's always possible that some of the death 
messages are no longer possible, since NetHack has had several releases 
since we started doing this.

We still think it's better to have a few no-longer-possible entries in 
there than to have to re-classify all deaths every year, so we 
definitely appreciate your pointing out ones that are out of date.

Now, on to the specific comments:

".* with a fake Amulet":
	I already changed this one to ".*(with a fake Amulet)".

"poisoned by a fall onto poison spikes":
	This one doesn't occur at all in last year's data, we see "killed by a 
fall onto poison spikes" instead (which is already in the file) so I'm 
cutting this one.

"poisoned by a poisoned blast":
	"blast" and "poison" don't  both occur in any entries from lat year, so 
I'm cutting this one too.

"using a magical horn on (him|her)self":
	The bare version doesn't show up in last year's data either (though 
only 4 of these deaths were logged), so I changed it to the "killed by" 
version.

There's a good chance that there are more like that last one in there, 
since the bare versions used to be more common, and seem to be getting 
changed to more verbose ("killed by " and suchlike) messages.

I'll try to get the time to add some code that checks to see how many 
deaths are in the file that haven't been achieved in the current 
Tournament to try to get a handle on how many entries are possibly ut of 
date.

